Q: return value of a method in php A: <p>The way you call <code>DBA_Insert</code> method shows that you don't assign returned value.
<code>$insertMsg</code> is just object instance  (variable that holds a pointer/link) of <code>dba</code> class and you call one of its methods. With proper names your code should like this: </p>

<pre><code>$dba = new dba();
$result = $dba-&gt;insert(...);
</code></pre>

<p>I've changed method name as well, because it will always belong to objects of dba class and your instance variable name should also be self explanatory.</p>

